---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { entity } from '../../config';
---

<Legal
  title="Privacy Policy - Cenovya Labs"
  description="How the cenovyalabs.com website handles data. It sets no cookies, runs no third-party trackers, and collects nothing you type."
  heading="Privacy Policy"
>
  <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
  <p>
    This site is operated by {entity.legalName}, {entity.legalDescriptor}. Questions about privacy:
    <a href={`mailto:${entity.emails.legal}`}>{entity.emails.legal}</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>2. What this policy covers</h2>
  <p>
    This policy covers the cenovyalabs.com website only. Our apps have their own privacy policies,
    which govern the data those apps handle:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="https://nutovia.app/privacy.html" rel="noopener">Nutovia privacy policy</a></li>
    <li><a href="https://hoofandclaw.org/privacy" rel="noopener">Hoof &amp; Claw privacy policy</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. What we collect</h2>
  <p>
    Nothing you type. There are no accounts, no forms, and no newsletter on this site.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    We use Cloudflare Web Analytics, which is cookieless. It records aggregate page views, referring
    site, country, and device type. It sets no cookies, does not fingerprint your browser, and does
    not follow you to other sites. We cannot identify you from it.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Hosting logs</h2>
  <p>
    The site is served by Cloudflare, which processes IP addresses in order to deliver and protect
    the site. This is a standard hosting function and that data is handled under Cloudflare's own
    policies.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Email</h2>
  <p>
    If you email us, we receive your address and whatever you write. We keep it only as long as
    needed to answer you and handle any follow-up.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Cookies</h2>
  <p>This site sets none.</p>

  <h2>8. Sharing and selling</h2>
  <p>
    We do not sell or share personal information. There are no advertising networks, trackers, or
    third-party pixels on this site.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    California residents may request access to, correction of, or deletion of personal information we
    hold. Email <a href={`mailto:${entity.emails.legal}`}>{entity.emails.legal}</a> and we will
    respond as required by law. In practice this site holds nothing about you unless you have emailed
    us.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    If this policy changes, the effective date above changes with it. Material changes will be noted
    on this page.
  </p>
</Legal>
